ing vaccinated and despite the  cdc guidelines now saying you know  vaccinated people really don't have to  wear masks  in most situations including indoors  let's take a look at this segment  but the president is saying a lot by  showing us what he's wearing we have  some new video you can see  at a electric vehicle plant in dearborn  michigan he has got a face mask  covering his mouth and nose which  conflicts with the cdc guidance that  you don't have to do that or socially  distance indoors or outdoors as long as  you are vaccinated  which the president has been since  before taking the oath of office  now when it comes to that specific event  with joe biden  at the ford plant and i believe it was  michigan remember that the cdc  guidelines are not state policy  and the cdc guidelines have not yet been  made state policy in many places and  state policy and state law  supersede recommendations from the cdc  at the end of the day they're just  recommendations  and of course ford it's not just  michigan ford may well still have a  policy  that everybody's masking indoors  regardless of vaccination status  many retailers still do etc but  fundamentally putting that aside  who cares if other people want to wear  masks as i've said before  i don't believe the outdoor masks were  ever really necessary  in almost any situation but i did it in  order to be a team player  because those were the cdc guidelines  and or  state guidelines and as soon as the cdc  said masks are no longer recommended  outdoors for vaccinated people  i haven't worn my mask outdoors since  other than in specific situations like  waiting in line to get into a grocery  store where the grocery store recommends  it  now that the cdc has said basically  every activity for vaccinated people is  low risk  i'm seeing other vaccinated people and  the truth is  everybody i know is vaccinated at this  point but i'm seeing vaccinated people  indoors we're not wearing masks i've  even sat inside of some cafes  but when i see people outside wearing a  mask i don't care i don't give it two  seconds of thought  if i if i devote some thought to it i  might wonder well  maybe they're not yet vaccinated okay so  they're wearing a mask  maybe they have a particular situation  medically  where they are at risk or maybe they  just like covering their face or maybe  they're afraid because it's been 14  months of this and it takes time for  people to readjust  or whatever who cares just because it's  not the cdc recommendation and just  because i'm not doing it what do i care  if other people are doing it  as long as they're not berating me to do  something that is not part of the cdc  recommendation so this is yet another  one of those instances  in which the hypocritical right wingers  claim to have certain values  but they don't stand by them when the  rubber meets the road  now the other reality we also should  mention  is that any guidelines where there is a  degree of nuance  where you need more than one sentence  it's probably too complicated for the  people that watch  fox news so it wouldn't be surprising to  me if the reason  imagine that we looked and like maybe  michigan has pulled the  mask mandate and maybe ford did too i  don't know it looks like everybody was  wearing a mask there so ford probably  requires it but imagine that ford said  you don't have to wear masks if you're  vaccinated michigan said the same thing  if fox news viewers turn on the tv  and absent any context they just see joe  biden walking around with no mask  many of them are going to immediately  take their masks off in all situations  even around vaccinated people because  they don't understand what the hell is  going on so  in some sense you could make the case it  makes a lot of sense for the president  of the u.s  to keep wearing the mask when he's going  to appear on tv and in public  so that unvaccinated fox viewers don't  see it and assume  they're clear to just do whatever the  hell the